{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QHeatEquationUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QHeatEquationUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QAnalysis"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QHeatEquation.unique_solution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QHeatEquation.unique_solution","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation-unique.lean#L34-L46","doc":"**Uniqueness of the q-heat time-derivative (proved).**\n\nTwo `QHeatEquation S` instances with the same q-Laplacian image\n`dq_u` have the same time-derivative `dt_u`: the evolution\nequation `dt_u t x = -dq_u t x` determines it pointwise.  This\nreplaces an unchecked external axiom with the determination the\nevolution equation genuinely provides. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-heat-equation-unique","label":"prop:q-heat-equation-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}